    "details": "Microsoft's FOSS Fund provides cash sponsorships to open source projects nominated and selected by Microsoft employees. It is an employee nomination program, not a public grant application: maintainers cannot submit an application themselves.\n\n**Project criteria and nomination.** The project must be used by Microsoft, have an OSI-approved open source license, and have a way to receive funds acceptable to Microsoft's procurement and legal teams; Microsoft says GitHub Sponsors is preferred. A project cannot be owned by a Microsoft employee. Microsoft employees and interns may nominate projects. During each round's stated voting period, employees who contributed to an open source project can vote; Microsoft describes GitHub pull requests, issues and reviews as qualifying contributions, with a self-attestation route for other technical or non-technical contributions. Nominators are encouraged to prioritize diversity, equity and inclusion.\n\n**Funding and availability.** Microsoft's repository says a quarterly fund distributes up to $12,500 across one or more projects and describes selected projects as receiving up to $12,500. It does not publish a typical award or allocation formula, so the amount for any project is uncertain. The repository says nominations are accepted daily and selections are made quarterly; its latest listed round is FOSS Fund 36 (March 2026). The public materials do not provide a maintainer application route, a direct public nomination form, decision timeline, or detailed payment terms.\n\nSee Microsoft's [FOSS Fund repository](https://github.com/microsoft/foss-fund) for criteria, process and recipient rounds, and its [Open Source Ecosystem page](https://opensource.microsoft.com/ecosystem/) for Microsoft's current description of employee selection.\n\nFees (OSS.Fund): The reviewed program pages do not publish applicant or recipient fees. They also do not detail payment administration or tax terms.\n\nImported from OSS.Fund on 2026-11-02 under CC BY 4.0. Canonical listing: https://www.oss.fund/microsoft-foss-fund/",
